=============================================================
  Estimated Parameters and Standard Deviations
=============================================================

  nabla Y_t = alpha (beta'Y_{t-1} - E[W]) + Gamma_1 nabla Y_{t-1} + ... + Theta(L) A_t
  with Pi = alpha beta' of rank r, and beta = [I_r ; beta_2] normalised on Y1.
  Johansen's notation throughout: a NEGATIVE alpha is error-correcting.
  Rows read `equation <- regressor`; D.x is nabla x, A.x its innovation,
  and ec is the equilibrium error beta'Y_{t-1}.

Parameter                         Estimate    Std.Error   t-stat   p-val
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mean of the equilibrium error (the constant restricted to the relation)
  E[ec1]                          8.286982     0.087125   95.116  0.0000 ***

Adjustment coefficients, alpha (M x r)   [negative = error-correcting]
  D.muskrat <- ec1               -0.286661     0.124674   -2.299  0.0215 *
  D.mink <- ec1                  -0.328017     0.124349   -2.638  0.0083 **

Cointegrating vectors, beta = [I_r ; beta_2], normalised on the Y1 block
  beta_2 held fixed: imposed, not estimated

Short-run dynamics, Gamma(k) on nabla Y_{t-k}
  D.muskrat <- D.muskrat(-1)      0.297488     0.130770    2.275  0.0229 *
